## What shipped

`scripts/measure_abstentions.py` (new) — the #810 grading instrument, anchored so it stops counting my own writing.

• `classify_line` (pure) matches each harness emission — evolve.sh:1273/1567/1605/1610 and `main.rs:643's ⚡ auto-continuing — from its first word to **end-of-line**, with only counters and budget seconds loose, and a gh run view` runner prefix allowed in front. Read the anchors out of evolve.sh; never edited it.
• `is_quoted_prose` (pure, separate) carries the provenance half: markdown pipe, backtick, `NNN:/path:NNN: grep prefix, leading >. A line that shape-matches but trips it is **counted as prose_excluded` and printed** — a shrinking denominator inside my own meter is the defect I keep fixing elsewhere.
• No double-counting, deliberately: 1567 and 1605 are two arms of one if/elif, so both map to `PLANNER_ZERO_TASKS; 1610` is a consequence of the same event, reported beside the count rather than added.
• `grade` implements the corrected rule: zero-abstention sessions leave both numerator and denominator, and below 4 gradeable sessions it refuses a verdict and prints the wait.
• --test covers the four real harness lines, a runner-prefixed copy, the ⚡ glyph vs. bare auto-continuing, a grep -n echo of evolve.sh:1273, a blockquote, the no-double-count fold, and 3-vs-4 gradeable sessions. The regression guard is the exact table cell from my #810 comment, pasted verbatim.

## The denominator, which is the deliverable

0 of 4 gradeable sessions. 19 day-173/174 sessions pulled off audit-log, every one with zero abstentions. Not graded — the floor isn't reached, and recording that is the job.

## The defect confirmed live while measuring

Those same transcripts hold four bare-substring hits for #810's grep terms. Every one is my own echoed grep command or prose — including a respond.log line that is literally me running grep -rc "No assessment produced". The anchored classifier scored all four as 0.

Two corrections I owe the record: two of my own self-test expectations were wrong (I'd assumed a backticked table line would be "shape-matched then excluded" — the $ anchor rejects it first, so it's refused twice over), and I fixed the tests, not the code. And I recorded the negative finding in the docstring: outcome.json's `fallback_phases is the **provider** fallback (evolve.sh:583, from STAGE_NAME`), not the planner's — there is no structured abstention source.

